#!/bin/sh
# summary: name every record that breaks its container's current declaration, or with --leftovers what the store's storage holds beyond its keys, and with --sweep clear it
# usage: ctx store check <container> | --leftovers [--sweep [--dry-run] [--delete]]
# help: prints one line per record and field, <container>/<id>: <field>: <reason>, for a required field absent, a value outside its one-of set, a shape other than the declared one, or a leftover field the declaration no longer names; declarations change forward only, so a record breaking a later declaration is fixed by its next write (set, or --unset=<field> for a leftover)
# help: --leftovers reads the store's own storage instead, a whole read only walk through the storage layer's probe: one line per kind found beyond the records' keys, root: <kind>: <count> (<bytes> bytes), the kinds stray files, folders outside the key shape, empty folders (one an older release left after a container drop; a drop now removes its folder with its last record), symbolic links, special files, unreadable folders, lock or write remnants, keys the key rule refuses (a file named as a record whose name the key rule refuses), and names holding a newline (counted with their bytes, never parsed); it names no path and removes nothing; a driver that keeps no file tree refuses rc 2 (ERR_CAPABILITY_UNSUPPORTED)
# help: --leftovers --sweep clears it through the storage layer's sweep: every kind beyond the records' keys moved into a backup stamped for the run, or with --delete removed outright with no backup kept, a folder holding no record below it moved or removed whole as one item and counted as emptied, a record or declaration never touched; a folder it cannot read or enter is never moved or removed, in either form, nor any folder above it, but left untouched and named; a name holding a newline in its reach refuses the sweep rc 2, the dry run too, since the sweep never parses such a name; it prints one line per kind swept, root: <kind>: <count> (<bytes> bytes), root: folders emptied: <n> and root: unreadable folders left: <n> when any, then one closing line: swept: moved <n> items (<bytes> bytes) into the backup stamped <stamp> and emptied <e> folders, swept: deleted ... with no backup kept, or swept: nothing beyond the documents; nothing moved, a line ending , leaving <n> unreadable folders untouched (their rights need fixing) when the sweep left any (swept: nothing moved, leaving ... when only those remain); a second run moves nothing
# help: --sweep --dry-run takes no lock, writes nothing, and prints the same lines, its closing line saying what the run would do (dry run: would move ...); the human's word comes before a sweep, the dry run first
# help: exit codes: 0 every record conforms, nothing lies beyond the keys (nothing printed), or the sweep or its dry run completed; 1 a record does not, something lies beyond the keys, or a usage error (--dry-run or --delete without --sweep among them); an undeclared or dropped container rc 1 (ERR_ENTITY_NOT_FOUND); 2 a storage failure (a name holding a newline in the sweep's reach, or an item the sweep cannot move or remove, which stops it, its line naming the kind and the items swept before it, which stay swept)
# help: example: ctx store check notes
# help: example: ctx store check --leftovers --sweep --dry-run
dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
exec "$dir/store" check "$@"
